$ otman --help
exit: 0
-- stdout --
Run an Obsidian Vault as an issue tracker

Usage:
  otman [flags]
  otman [command]

Available Commands:
  close       Close an Item
  config      Show or change user config
  create      Create an Item in the selected Project
  help        Help about any command
  list        List the Items of the selected Project (default: open ones)
  project     Create, list, view and link Projects
  reopen      Reopen a closed Item
  view        Show an Item by ID, number, full filename or Vault-relative path

Flags:
      --actor string     actor name (overrides OTM_ACTOR and config)
      --format string    output format: human|axi|json (default human on a terminal, axi otherwise)
  -h, --help             help for otman
      --json             shorthand for --format json
      --project string   Project key (overrides OTM_PROJECT and config)
      --vault string     Vault path (overrides OTM_VAULT and config)
  -v, --version          version for otman

Use "otman [command] --help" for more information about a command.
-- stderr --

